      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RODNEY OH RODNEY (4) gets the nod first-up after closing his last campaign with a narrow Belmont Park fifth on heavy ground, beaten just over a length after racing keenly enough in front. His Bunbury Class 5 win from Salty Miss two runs ago gives him the strongest winning reference, and his record at 1200m, along with three wins from seven starts with this jockey, makes him the one they have to beat. STORM LORD (5) is the main danger after a sound Ascot fifth in 1 Metro Win grade, beaten just over two lengths, and his Bunbury third prior showed he is holding his form despite starting at long odds. MARS MISSION (3) has to rebound from a flat Ascot ninth, but his Moora win over WEAPONS HOT reads well and he has won twice this season. WEAPONS HOT (2) was close up at Ascot despite being unwanted, has a prior win at this venue, and the quick back-up keeps him in the each-way mix. WUIGI (6) won't be far away.",
